  "live_records": {
    "q-130033": {
      "dom_id": "step-q130033",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.45),$ compute $P(X=4).$  Round your final answer to $4$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.45),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(0.55)}^{x-1}(0.45), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=4) & =f(4) \\\\  & ={(0.55)}^{3}(0.45) \\\\  & ≈0.0749.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
