    "q-332366": {
      "dom_id": "step-q332366",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{1}{2}),$ compute $P(X=6).$  Round your final answer to $4$ decimal places.\n\n$P(X=6)≈$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{1}{2}),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{x-1}(\\frac{1}{2}), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=6) & =f(6) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{2})}^{5}(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & ≈0.0156.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
