    "q-331515": {
      "dom_id": "step-q331515",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{1}{5}),$ compute the **exact** value of $P(X=4).$\n\n$P(X=4)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{1}{5}),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{4}{5})}^{x-1}(\\frac{1}{5}), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=4) & =f(4) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{4}{5})}^{3}(\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{64}{625}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
