    "q-335472": {
      "dom_id": "step-q335472",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{3}{4}),$ compute the **exact** value of $P(X<5).$\n\n$P(X<5)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{3}{4}),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{x-1}(\\frac{3}{4}), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<5) & =P(X\\in \\{1,2,3,4\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2)+P(X=3)+P(X=4) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3)+f(4) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{4})}^{0}(\\frac{3}{4})+{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{1}(\\frac{3}{4})+{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}(\\frac{3}{4})+{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{3}(\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{255}{256}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
