    "q-97139": {
      "dom_id": "step-q97139",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.3),$ compute $P(X\\le 4).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.3),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(0.7)}^{x-1}(0.3), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 4) & =P(X\\in \\{1,2,3,4\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2)+P(X=3)+P(X=4) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3)+f(4) \\\\  & ={(0.7)}^{0}(0.3)+{(0.7)}^{1}(0.3)+{(0.7)}^{2}(0.3)+{(0.7)}^{3}(0.3) \\\\  & =0.7599.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
