    "q-97142": {
      "dom_id": "step-q97142",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.95),$ compute $P(X<4).$  Round your final answer to $4$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.95),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(0.05)}^{x-1}(0.95), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<4) & =P(X\\in \\{1,2,3\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2)+P(X=3) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3) \\\\  & ={(0.05)}^{0}(0.95)+{(0.05)}^{1}(0.95)+{(0.05)}^{2}(0.95) \\\\  & ≈0.9999.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
