    "q-329137": {
      "dom_id": "step-q329137",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.75),$ compute $P(X<5).$ Round your final answer to $4$ decimal places.\n\n$P(X<5)≈$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.75),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(0.25)^{x-1}(0.75), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<5) & =P(X\\in \\{1,2,3\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2)+P(X=3)+P(X=4) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3)+f(4) \\\\  & =(0.25)^{0}(0.75)+(0.25)^{1}(0.75)+(0.25)^{2}(0.75)+(0.25)^{3}(0.75) \\\\  & ≈0.9961.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
