    "q-332934": {
      "dom_id": "step-q332934",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{3}{5}),$ compute the **exact** value of $P(3\\le X\\le 6).$\n\n$P(3\\le X\\le 6)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{3}{5}),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{2}{5})}^{x-1}(\\frac{3}{5}), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3\\le X\\le 6) & =P(X\\in \\{3,4,5,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=3)+P(X=4)+P(X=5)+P(X=6) \\\\  & =f(3)+f(4)+f(5)+f(6) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2}{5})}^{2}(\\frac{3}{5})+{(\\frac{2}{5})}^{3}(\\frac{3}{5})+{(\\frac{2}{5})}^{4}(\\frac{3}{5})+{(\\frac{2}{5})}^{5}(\\frac{3}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2436}{15625}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
