      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Given that $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.25),$ compute $P(3\\le X<7)$ rounded to $4$ decimal places.\n\n$P(3\\le X<7)≈$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.25),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(0.75)^{x-1}(0.25), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3\\le X<7) & =P(X\\in \\{3,4,5,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=3)+P(X=4)+P(X=5)+P(X=6) \\\\  & =f(3)+f(4)+f(5)+f(6) \\\\  & =(0.75)^{2}(0.25)+(0.75)^{3}(0.25)+(0.75)^{4}(0.25)+(0.75)^{5}(0.25) \\\\  & ≈0.3845.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
