    "q-97164": {
      "dom_id": "step-q97164",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Given that $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{5}{12}),$ compute $P(4<X<7)$ rounded to $4$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{5}{12}),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{7}{12})}^{x-1}(\\frac{5}{12}), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(4<X<7) & =P(X\\in \\{5,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=5)+P(X=6) \\\\  & =f(5)+f(6) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{7}{12})}^{4}(\\frac{5}{12})+{(\\frac{7}{12})}^{5}(\\frac{5}{12}) \\\\  & ≈0.0764.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
