    "q-97154": {
      "dom_id": "step-q97154",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Given that $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{1}{7}),$ compute $P(5\\le X<8)$ rounded to $4$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{1}{7}),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{6}{7})}^{x-1}(\\frac{1}{7}), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(5\\le X<8) & =P(X\\in \\{5,6,7\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=5)+P(X=6)+P(X=7) \\\\  & =f(5)+f(6)+f(7) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{6}{7})}^{4}(\\frac{1}{7})+{(\\frac{6}{7})}^{5}(\\frac{1}{7})+{(\\frac{6}{7})}^{6}(\\frac{1}{7}) \\\\  & ≈0.1999.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
