    "q-97152": {
      "dom_id": "step-q97152",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Given that $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.72),$ compute $P(6\\le X\\le 10)$ rounded to $4$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.72),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(0.28)}^{x-1}(0.72), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(6\\le X\\le 10) & =P(X\\in \\{6,7,8,9,10\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=6)+P(X=7)+P(X=8)+P(X=9)+P(X=10) \\\\  & =f(6)+f(7)+f(8)+f(9)+f(10) \\\\  & ={(0.28)}^{5}(0.72)+{(0.28)}^{6}(0.72)+{(0.28)}^{7}(0.72)+{(0.28)}^{8}(0.72)+{(0.28)}^{9}(0.72) \\\\  & ≈0.0017.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-97152-a",
