    "q-335508": {
      "dom_id": "step-q335508",
      "name": "Question 17",
      "problem": "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{7}{8}),$ compute $P(X\\ge 3)$ round to $4$ decimal places.\n\n$P(X\\ge 3)≈$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{7}{8}),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{1}{8})}^{x-1}(\\frac{7}{8}), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are infinitely many values of $X$ such that $X\\ge 3.$ However, we can simplify the computation by using the complement instead:\n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 3)=1-P(X<3)\n$$\n\nComputing the complement, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<3) & =P(X\\in \\{1,2\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{8})}^{0}(\\frac{7}{8})+{(\\frac{1}{8})}^{1}(\\frac{7}{8}) \\\\  & =0.984375.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 3) & =1-P(X<3) \\\\  & =1-0.984375 \\\\  & ≈0.0156.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
