    "q-276116": {
      "dom_id": "step-q276116",
      "name": "Question 19",
      "problem": "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.8),$ compute the **exact** value of $P(X>3).$\n\n$P(X>3)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.9),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(0.2)^{x-1}(0.8), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are infinitely many values of $X$ such that $X>3.$ However, we can simplify the computation by using the complement instead:\n\n$$\nP(X>3)=1-P(X\\le 3)\n$$\n\nComputing the complement, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 3) & =P(X\\in \\{1,2,3\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2)+P(X=3) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3) \\\\  & =(0.2)^{0}(0.8)+(0.2)^{1}(0.8)+(0.2)^{2}(0.8) \\\\  & =0.992.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>3) & =1-P(X\\le 3) \\\\  & =1-0.992 \\\\  & =0.008.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
