      "name": "Question 20",
      "problem": "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{5}{7}),$ compute $P(X\\ge 3)$ rounded to $4$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{5}{7}),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{2}{7})}^{x-1}(\\frac{5}{7}), & x=1,2,3… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are infinitely many values of $X$ such that $X\\ge 3.$ However, we can simplify the computation by using the complement instead:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 3) & =1-P(X<3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the complement, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<3) & =P(X\\in \\{1,2\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2}{7})}^{0}(\\frac{5}{7})+{(\\frac{2}{7})}^{1}(\\frac{5}{7}) \\\\  & ≈0.9184.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 3) & =1-P(X<3) \\\\  & ≈1-0.9184 \\\\  & =0.0816.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
